WEBVTT

00:03.094 --> 00:04.204
Well.

00:04.204 --> 00:06.434
An Abh cat with a good pedigree.

00:06.434 --> 00:07.904
A Kutirowaru?

00:08.704 --> 00:10.974
Let me give you some advice.

00:10.974 --> 00:12.574
If you're going to
keep him onboard...

00:12.574 --> 00:15.134
...you should have a
transmitter on his collar.

00:15.714 --> 00:17.244
That is, if you don't want him...

00:17.244 --> 00:20.544
...to suffer anything traumatic
in the event of a pressure leak.

00:22.084 --> 00:24.424
Nice and meaty!

00:24.424 --> 00:26.124
Hey, kid.

00:26.124 --> 00:28.424
You're the supply officer,
aren't you?

00:28.854 --> 00:32.394
Now, bringing a cat like this onboard...

00:32.394 --> 00:35.054
...we have an excellent officer here!

00:38.004 --> 00:40.334
The senior aviator told me.

00:40.704 --> 00:42.264
I think you'll find this will help.

00:42.874 --> 00:43.634
This?

00:43.844 --> 00:45.034
It's a transmitter.

00:47.214 --> 00:49.614
I don't know what to say
about your lack of sense.

00:50.214 --> 00:51.904
We're going into battle soon.

00:52.314 --> 00:55.184
Don't you think it's unfair
having him here?

00:55.884 --> 00:57.714
But what can I do?

00:57.954 --> 01:01.414
The Basroil's my home.

01:01.894 --> 01:06.884
The Shapes of Bonds

01:10.804 --> 01:12.764
Are you still alive, Jinto?

01:37.794 --> 01:39.264
You know...

01:39.264 --> 01:42.284
...you look like a fool
even when you're asleep.

01:42.764 --> 01:46.254
Wouldn't "unconscious" be
a better way to describe it?

01:48.174 --> 01:50.604
I was dreaming of everyone.

01:50.974 --> 01:54.234
And the body of Klasbul
was lying in his coffin.

01:55.944 --> 01:59.434
I never imagined I'd experience
being a corpse while still alive.

01:59.744 --> 02:01.184
Does it still hurt?

02:01.714 --> 02:02.944
It's just a scratch.

02:04.524 --> 02:06.024
It's humiliating.

02:06.024 --> 02:10.594
To ride a ship with no exterior
area sensors or guhakes.

02:10.594 --> 02:12.324
This is not a ship.

02:12.324 --> 02:13.594
It's a coffin.

02:13.964 --> 02:15.324
C-O-F-F-I-N.

02:15.494 --> 02:19.224
It's cramped in here.
I suddenly feel annoyed by you.

02:19.504 --> 02:20.994
- Stay away from me.
- Ouch!

02:21.474 --> 02:23.764
Be careful. I'm injured.

02:24.044 --> 02:25.594
I thought it was a scratch.

02:27.944 --> 02:28.974
Jinto.

02:28.974 --> 02:30.184
Yeah?

02:30.184 --> 02:31.144
Forgive me.

02:31.784 --> 02:32.744
For what?

02:33.014 --> 02:35.144
You are...

02:36.684 --> 02:38.214
...an honorable man.

02:38.924 --> 02:40.484
What is it, Jinto?

02:41.454 --> 02:42.694
Uh, nothing.

02:42.694 --> 02:45.494
This emergency pod is more
comfortable than the coffin.

02:45.964 --> 02:48.554
But it only gives us
twenty-four hours.

02:48.834 --> 02:51.264
I'm sure Sobaash will have
rescued us before then.

02:51.964 --> 02:53.194
Of course she will!

02:53.904 --> 02:55.474
Why are you so angry?

02:55.474 --> 02:56.634
I'm not angry.

02:58.744 --> 03:00.214
What's so funny?

03:00.214 --> 03:03.074
Nothing.
When you get angry like that...

03:03.074 --> 03:06.514
...I feel kind of relieved.
I wonder why.

03:11.224 --> 03:12.524
Can I pick him up?

03:12.524 --> 03:14.254
He looks like he needs exercise.

03:15.094 --> 03:18.494
Oh, sure. Guess I've been
a neglectful owner.

03:18.494 --> 03:19.664
Tell that to the cat.

03:19.664 --> 03:23.634
He's fine. He neglects me as well,
so we've got a lot in common.

03:23.634 --> 03:24.254
I see.

03:26.804 --> 03:28.034
He'll come back.

03:28.504 --> 03:32.044
I guess I've got nowhere
I can call home now.

03:32.044 --> 03:32.904
Jinto.

03:33.874 --> 03:39.074
O Stars, listen to our plea
as our lives are but short.

03:39.984 --> 03:41.414
Our wish...

03:41.414 --> 03:45.644
...is that you will guide us to you
when we meet our end.

03:46.624 --> 03:48.314
It's strange.

03:48.694 --> 03:52.124
It almost feels like
nothing matters anymore.

03:54.164 --> 03:57.294
Maybe it's because I'm with you.

03:57.634 --> 03:58.434
You fool.

03:59.234 --> 04:01.934
I wonder who...

04:02.774 --> 04:03.704
...I really am.

04:07.944 --> 04:09.314
And then...

04:09.314 --> 04:11.414
...we were rescued...

04:11.414 --> 04:15.144
...twelve hours after the
Basroil was destroyed.

04:20.424 --> 04:22.754
How was your bath?

04:22.754 --> 04:24.594
It wasn't too bad.

04:24.864 --> 04:28.524
Although the water splashed
on my face at every shot.

04:28.734 --> 04:30.894
Any change in the situation?

04:31.504 --> 04:32.994
Nothing, really.

04:33.204 --> 04:35.134
Except that the enemy retreated.

04:36.004 --> 04:38.664
And it appears that the
main fleet has arrived.

04:39.374 --> 04:40.394
What did you say?!

04:40.774 --> 04:43.374
Why didn't you inform me
of something so important?!

04:43.744 --> 04:48.444
Even as a kid, you'd get upset
if your bath was disturbed.

04:48.684 --> 04:51.114
Only if I was disturbed
for no reason.

04:51.754 --> 04:53.774
It's different when there's
something important going on.

04:54.194 --> 04:55.484
I'll remember that.

04:56.354 --> 04:59.354
But it wouldn't have meant anything
even if I did tell you.

04:59.824 --> 05:02.854
As commander-in-chief,
I'll decide that.

05:04.204 --> 05:06.034
Now, let's go after the enemy!

05:07.274 --> 05:09.704
I figured that's what you'd say.

05:10.244 --> 05:12.704
That's why I didn't tell you.

05:12.704 --> 05:13.804
What?

05:13.974 --> 05:15.944
Our fleet is in really bad shape.

05:16.244 --> 05:19.744
If we go after them now,
we'll just end up getting routed.

05:19.744 --> 05:21.234
That wouldn't happen...

05:29.354 --> 05:32.294
All right. You win this time, Nefee.

05:32.294 --> 05:34.534
It's not a matter of win or lose.

05:34.534 --> 05:36.394
We have to regroup...

05:36.394 --> 05:39.504
...and hope that the main fleet
is victorious over the enemy.

05:39.504 --> 05:41.904
That's all we can do?

05:41.904 --> 05:43.334
What're you talking about?

05:43.334 --> 05:45.234
It's not an easy task.

05:45.444 --> 05:48.974
Although we, the staff, are the ones
who do the actual work.

05:48.974 --> 05:50.484
By the way, Nereis...

05:50.484 --> 05:51.134
What now?

05:51.984 --> 05:53.674
You might as well
go back to your bath.

05:56.514 --> 05:58.184
Enemy one has now
achieved space-time fusion!

05:58.184 --> 06:00.494
Prepare the electromagnetic
cannons!

06:00.494 --> 06:01.454
Enemy detected!

06:01.454 --> 06:02.394
Cannons ready!

06:02.394 --> 06:05.324
Armor damaged! Sectors
4, 11, 15!

06:05.324 --> 06:07.024
Pressure leak!

06:07.164 --> 06:08.994
Jettison the armor!

06:14.204 --> 06:15.974
That's just like Beneej.

06:15.974 --> 06:18.674
She's taken a merciless
and devastating tactic.

06:18.674 --> 06:22.874
Rather crude, even for an Abriel.

06:23.314 --> 06:27.614
Whatever she may be, her fighting
style is crude and overly violent.

06:28.014 --> 06:31.654
But her strategy is proving
to be extremely effective.

06:31.654 --> 06:32.984
Do me a favor.

06:32.984 --> 06:37.124
Please avoid giving any praise
to the head of the Spoor family...

06:37.124 --> 06:39.284
...within the range of my senses.

06:39.724 --> 06:41.954
It's not really praise.

06:42.434 --> 06:44.164
Merely a realistic observation.

06:44.764 --> 06:46.754
We've got the enemy
in disarray as a result.

06:47.104 --> 06:49.464
Even our side is in disarray.

07:05.754 --> 07:07.954
We're passing through the rear
of the enemy formation now.

07:07.954 --> 07:09.954
Maybe we went too quickly.

07:09.954 --> 07:10.354
Huh?

07:11.564 --> 07:13.254
She regrets it.

07:13.594 --> 07:14.394
Yes.

07:14.394 --> 07:17.504
Most of our squadrons will reach
the rear of the enemy fleet shortly.

07:17.504 --> 07:20.994
But only two squadrons have
managed to keep pace with us.

07:21.374 --> 07:23.434
Maybe we should
take a little break?

07:23.434 --> 07:26.344
I think it would be
prudent to do that.

07:26.604 --> 07:28.234
Then let's do that.

07:28.844 --> 07:30.744
Inform all of my ships.

07:30.744 --> 07:32.914
Put their space-time bubbles
into stationary mode.

07:32.914 --> 07:33.954
However...

07:33.954 --> 07:36.554
...should a situation arise
where it is necessary to move...

07:36.554 --> 07:39.814
...give them permission to mobilize
their space-time bubbles.

07:40.154 --> 07:41.124
Understood, ma'am.

07:43.794 --> 07:47.594
It's a good thing the enemy has
used up their supply of mines.

07:48.394 --> 07:51.334
They must've been very confident
that they would capture Aptic.

07:51.634 --> 07:53.364
That's probably not
the only reason.

07:53.604 --> 07:58.044
They were probably confident
in their new fleet formations.

07:58.344 --> 07:59.634
That may be so.

08:01.744 --> 08:03.714
Contact the ships in the Assault
Vessel Mudoto Contingent.

08:04.344 --> 08:06.784
Tell them to pull out of
the battlefield immediately.

08:07.044 --> 08:08.714
Their losses are too great.

08:08.714 --> 08:09.984
Yes, sir.

08:10.214 --> 08:12.714
The same goes for Konaseeru
and Garikoosh.

08:12.954 --> 08:16.444
That means eleven squadrons
will have been withdrawn.

08:16.724 --> 08:20.124
I was prepared for some losses.
But this is terrible.

08:21.064 --> 08:23.194
I'm afraid it is terrible.

08:23.194 --> 08:24.424
Actually, Your Highness...

08:24.734 --> 08:26.724
I think you're doing rather well.

08:26.964 --> 08:30.264
Although they had more ships,
we've controlled the battlefield.

08:30.504 --> 08:32.164
I wonder about that.

08:32.674 --> 08:34.974
If those other two fleets
were to arrive soon...

08:34.974 --> 08:37.284
...our situation would
improve considerably.

08:37.284 --> 08:40.344
You mean Admiral Rulef's
Second Fleet...

08:40.344 --> 08:42.944
...and Admiral Kotoponi's
Fourth Fleet?

08:44.384 --> 08:46.754
I wonder what
those two are doing.

08:47.354 --> 08:49.054
What do you mean?

08:49.054 --> 08:51.424
They're advancing as fast
as physics will allow them.

08:51.594 --> 08:55.654
It seems like they're advancing
as quickly as possible.

08:56.494 --> 08:59.934
I sometimes despise physics.

09:02.504 --> 09:03.604
Oh, Your Highness...

09:03.604 --> 09:07.104
As your loyal chief of staff...

09:07.104 --> 09:10.344
...I suppose I'm to
ignore that last comment?

09:10.614 --> 09:11.744
Yes.

09:11.744 --> 09:15.384
I don't know exactly
to whom you are loyal.

09:15.384 --> 09:17.974
But if you could ignore
that comment, I'd appreciate it.

09:19.424 --> 09:21.854
I apologize for venting
my petty complaints.

09:21.854 --> 09:23.154
Not at all.

09:23.154 --> 09:24.364
Commander!

09:24.364 --> 09:26.524
There's a message from
the Second Fleet!

09:26.524 --> 09:27.864
It's Admiral Rulef!

09:31.604 --> 09:34.874
Distance to the enemy front
one hundred wesdaj!

09:34.874 --> 09:36.974
The First Fleet has
stopped advancing...

09:36.974 --> 09:38.774
...and now appears to be
gathering its forces.

09:38.774 --> 09:40.334
We've made it in time!

09:40.614 --> 09:42.514
The enemy appears
to be in disarray.

09:42.874 --> 09:43.884
All right.

09:43.884 --> 09:45.884
All ships!
Prepare to launch mines!

09:45.884 --> 09:48.574
We've got to make up
for lost time!

09:49.084 --> 09:51.174
All ships ready to launch mines!

09:51.884 --> 09:53.054
After deploying their mines...

09:53.054 --> 09:55.754
...all ships are to advance in
individual space-time bubbles.

09:55.754 --> 09:56.524
Yes, sir!

09:56.524 --> 09:57.664
All right!

09:57.664 --> 09:59.784
All mobile space-time mines! Fire!

10:02.334 --> 10:04.354
The Second Fleet is
attacking the enemy!

10:04.534 --> 10:06.234
Our break is over!

10:06.234 --> 10:07.574
Notify all ships!

10:07.574 --> 10:10.404
Mobilize their individual
space-time bubbles!

10:10.404 --> 10:11.904
Heading on a course of 270!

10:11.904 --> 10:15.304
Continuously transmit the message
to follow me!

10:16.744 --> 10:19.814
Can't wait to bully
these weaklings around!

10:19.814 --> 10:22.784
It's not exactly my idea of fun.

10:24.054 --> 10:25.154
She couldn't be...?!

10:25.154 --> 10:29.224
It's a little bit old-fashioned
but it seems so refreshing.

10:29.224 --> 10:31.524
She couldn't possibly say that!

10:32.994 --> 10:34.294
Now!

10:34.294 --> 10:36.334
You lousy pigs and mud turtles!

10:36.334 --> 10:37.824
Prepare to meet your doom!

10:38.634 --> 10:40.674
The Lashkau has entered
space-time fusion!

10:40.674 --> 10:43.294
The Seventh Attack Vessel Squadron!
Space-time fusion!

10:45.474 --> 10:47.134
Fire the electromagnetic cannon!

10:47.644 --> 10:50.014
Second Squadron Kuryuders!
Spread out!

10:50.014 --> 10:50.914
Roger!

10:50.914 --> 10:53.104
Leikross!
Attack from the right side!

10:57.384 --> 10:59.254
Coming about 180 degrees!

10:59.254 --> 11:00.814
Prepare to fire the
anti-proton cannon!

11:02.254 --> 11:04.224
Anti-proton cannon ready!

11:09.534 --> 11:11.804
Enemy three and enemy nine
are separating!

11:11.804 --> 11:12.734
Don't let them get away!

11:13.834 --> 11:16.204
Space-time bubbles approaching
ahead to port!

11:27.554 --> 11:28.884
It's the Fourth Fleet!

11:29.554 --> 11:31.114
Enemy nine destroyed!

11:31.684 --> 11:34.284
Fire the electromagnetic
cannon continuously.

11:35.224 --> 11:38.284
In addition to the Fourth Fleet...
other squadrons are now engaged!

11:38.964 --> 11:41.194
We now have an
overwhelming advantage.

11:41.694 --> 11:44.034
Now we will surely win.

11:44.034 --> 11:44.894
I think so.

11:45.864 --> 11:48.354
It appears the enemy is retreating
into the Wimpel region.

11:49.534 --> 11:51.374
What would you like to do now?

11:51.374 --> 11:53.604
When the enemy has
withdrawn into Wimpel...

11:53.604 --> 11:55.744
...we will seal them off
with front line ships.

11:55.744 --> 11:58.344
Then, once we've established
control of Aptic...

11:58.344 --> 12:00.714
...Mystel and Dalmav...

12:00.714 --> 12:03.914
...we'll move on and take
Neopol and Malskuty.

12:04.154 --> 12:07.354
And you plan to cut off any
remaining enemy forces?

12:08.294 --> 12:10.794
We'll let the Fifth Fleet
handle that.

12:10.794 --> 12:13.694
Then we'll be free to take over
more enemy territories.

12:14.264 --> 12:15.354
Understood.

12:15.634 --> 12:19.164
But there's just one
problem remaining.

12:19.164 --> 12:20.404
And what's that?

12:20.404 --> 12:22.704
I still don't know which one.

12:22.704 --> 12:25.934
Was it Nereis or was it Nefee?

12:26.674 --> 12:28.114
Which was it?!

12:28.114 --> 12:29.334
Your Highness!

12:29.574 --> 12:31.284
Don't tell me...

12:31.284 --> 12:33.844
...that it was both of them.

12:34.054 --> 12:38.284
Or perhaps you don't
know which one it was.

12:39.754 --> 12:41.124
Your Highness...

12:42.024 --> 12:46.014
I have devoted half my life
to the Star Forces.

12:46.594 --> 12:51.254
If there's anybody who doubts
your loyalty, bring them here.

12:51.664 --> 12:54.264
I'd be perfectly happy to
convince them otherwise.

12:55.304 --> 12:58.934
And I have the deepest love and
respect for the Imperial Family.

12:59.604 --> 13:02.164
That's very nice to hear.

13:02.614 --> 13:04.284
So, I ask...

13:04.284 --> 13:08.984
...that you understand that it is
difficult for me to say this to you...

13:08.984 --> 13:12.644
...the commanding admiral of the
Star Forces and heir to the throne.

13:13.384 --> 13:14.324
Yes?

13:15.254 --> 13:16.124
Just shut up!

13:16.124 --> 13:20.164
Imperial Calendar Year 955,
Month of Roswik, Day 23

13:20.164 --> 13:24.164
Battle of Aptic Gate Ends

13:24.164 --> 13:28.174
8779 Star Forces Vessels Destroyed

13:28.174 --> 13:31.674
211,055 Killed in Action

13:31.674 --> 13:36.134
The Government of the Aptic System
Announces its Surrender

13:39.584 --> 13:42.154
Vobeirunei Deity Ministry

13:42.154 --> 13:44.384
Vobeirunei Deity Ministry
It looks like I can get someone to
look after Diaho at the Clyuve Palace.

13:44.384 --> 13:45.944
It looks like I can get someone to
look after Diaho at the Clyuve Palace.

13:47.124 --> 13:50.354
I thought he was a pretty
friendly cat...

13:50.354 --> 13:53.594
...but he simply has no will
to do anything.

13:53.594 --> 13:54.584
Oh, really?

13:54.894 --> 13:57.604
I always wondered why you
two were so alike.

13:57.604 --> 14:00.304
Communication Ship Boorool
Now I think I understand why.

14:00.304 --> 14:00.704
Communication Ship Boorool

14:00.704 --> 14:01.894
Communication Ship Boorool
Don't say that.

14:03.674 --> 14:05.534
The docking is now complete.

14:05.944 --> 14:09.464
All personnel are requested
to prepare to embark.

14:10.574 --> 14:11.974
All right. Let's go.

14:12.414 --> 14:15.874
You've made proper arrangements
to send Diaho back to the capital?

14:16.284 --> 14:17.304
Of course!

14:17.654 --> 14:22.594
But I figured Ekuryua would
want to say goodbye to him.

14:23.394 --> 14:24.564
Trust me.

14:24.564 --> 14:27.024
I'll send him away after
we've finished the trials.

14:27.564 --> 14:29.964
I'm not going to forget
and leave him on the ship.

14:30.194 --> 14:31.704
Just make sure you don't.

14:31.704 --> 14:32.804
Understood?

14:32.804 --> 14:33.394
Okay.

14:34.474 --> 14:38.474
He'll probably forget
about me in no time.

14:38.474 --> 14:42.634
I don't think we should
expect a cat to remember us.

14:45.284 --> 14:46.174
Good advice.

14:47.484 --> 14:48.754
When you think about it...

14:48.754 --> 14:51.084
...in the time we spent
on the Basroil...

14:51.084 --> 14:53.414
...the only thing we fought
over was Diaho.

14:53.884 --> 14:56.624
It's weird to say this when
we're in the middle of a war.

14:56.624 --> 14:58.124
But things seem peaceful.

14:58.124 --> 15:00.064
That's only how you feel.

15:00.064 --> 15:01.934
And you say we fought
over Diaho...

15:01.934 --> 15:05.164
...but you never insisted that
we should keep him onboard.

15:05.734 --> 15:07.564
I suppose that's true.

15:08.104 --> 15:10.534
I mean, I did think
about saying something...

15:10.534 --> 15:13.874
...but it didn't seem appropriate
in the middle of a war.

15:14.444 --> 15:15.674
Fool.

15:16.114 --> 15:18.874
By the way, did you hear the
rumor about the new ships?

15:19.944 --> 15:21.434
Heavy attack vessels.

15:21.654 --> 15:23.774
I heard it was light patrol ships.

15:24.084 --> 15:27.074
Then maybe it's something
in between.

15:27.924 --> 15:30.484
I wonder why they're deploying
such awkward ships.

15:31.294 --> 15:34.524
Perhaps it's the attack vessels
that are awkward.

15:35.164 --> 15:39.534
Maybe there's no longer
any need for attack vessels.

15:40.334 --> 15:42.064
But I...

15:50.174 --> 15:52.374
Is that the new Basroil?

15:52.984 --> 15:54.844
It's the same as the last one.

15:55.054 --> 15:57.384
It's the same design.
What did you expect?

15:59.524 --> 16:01.954
Did you have a reason
for changing the subject?

16:01.954 --> 16:02.984
Huh?

16:03.194 --> 16:06.824
Uh, I thought that if the ship was
big enough, I could keep the cat.

16:07.524 --> 16:08.254
You fool.

16:10.064 --> 16:13.034
This inexperienced battleship...

16:13.304 --> 16:14.924
...was famous for
a peculiar reason.

16:15.934 --> 16:18.934
It was because two officers were
members of the nobility.

16:19.704 --> 16:24.384
One of them was our captain,
Abriel Nei Dubrusk Paryunu Lafiel.

16:24.384 --> 16:25.874
Or, Deca-Commander Abriel.

16:26.384 --> 16:30.684
Princess of one of the Royal Families
of the Humankind Empire Abh.

16:31.224 --> 16:34.054
The other was me...

16:34.054 --> 16:37.214
...Count Jinto of the Lin Syune
Rock Hyde family.

16:38.364 --> 16:42.054
This small ship was the only place
I could call home.

16:43.194 --> 16:46.424
And, if truth be told, it was the
only place where I felt I belonged.

16:49.174 --> 16:51.694
Captain. Supply Officer Lin.

16:53.474 --> 16:54.274
Welcome back.

16:59.414 --> 17:01.474
Captain, I would like
to return this to you.

17:02.014 --> 17:02.714
Thank you.

17:08.624 --> 17:11.424
This time I intend to fight better.

17:13.524 --> 17:15.194
I'll be counting on you again.

17:18.534 --> 17:21.234
Now! Let's prepare for departure!

17:24.234 --> 17:26.734
I'm the Empire's
Deputy Representative?!

17:27.444 --> 17:29.244
It's an order.

17:29.244 --> 17:30.234
You have no choice.

17:32.944 --> 17:37.754
The Aptic Planetary System and
territories of the United Mankind...

17:37.754 --> 17:42.394
...shall become a part of
the Humankind Empire Abh...

17:42.394 --> 17:47.124
...and shall fall under the laws
of the Empire as subject territories.

17:47.764 --> 17:49.534
If the Empire makes any demands
exceeding its own laws...

17:49.534 --> 17:51.534
Well, I didn't realize that...

17:51.534 --> 17:54.104
...such famous people were
under my command.

17:54.104 --> 17:55.904
When you have some time...

17:55.904 --> 18:00.404
...tell me the secret of how you can
be so ignorant about your fleet.

18:00.404 --> 18:02.174
Wasn't that Count Hyde...

18:02.174 --> 18:07.444
...the same one who conquered
some world with the Princess?

18:07.444 --> 18:08.484
"Conquered"?

18:08.484 --> 18:12.284
I heard he was able to
conquer a whole planet...

18:12.284 --> 18:14.274
...armed only with a laser gun.

18:15.224 --> 18:16.524
Hey, Nereis...

18:16.524 --> 18:18.894
...is there a problem with
your information...

18:18.894 --> 18:20.294
...or with your memory?

18:20.294 --> 18:22.834
I think you're pretty
far off the truth here.

18:22.834 --> 18:24.924
Who cares about the truth?

18:25.504 --> 18:28.774
I always find made-up stories
far more interesting.

18:28.774 --> 18:30.134
You could be right.

18:30.134 --> 18:34.474
But it's that attitude that
brings our reputation down.

18:35.374 --> 18:39.714
Do you intend
to take any action whatsoever...

18:39.714 --> 18:41.914
...to achieve independence
from the Empire?

18:42.354 --> 18:43.384
No...

18:43.384 --> 18:47.284
...but I might permit myself
to imagine it once in a while.

18:47.284 --> 18:48.844
Or is that forbidden?

18:52.664 --> 18:54.394
Depressurization complete.

18:54.394 --> 18:55.864
Release the locks on the gates!

18:56.064 --> 18:57.064
So.

18:57.064 --> 19:00.434
You've been released from your
duties as Territorial Ambassador?

19:01.104 --> 19:02.604
It's a shame.

19:02.604 --> 19:07.104
You're lucky you can continue to
take part in the battle operations.

19:07.104 --> 19:08.544
We, on the other hand...

19:08.544 --> 19:12.114
...have to complete the trials on
our new ship before we join you.

19:12.114 --> 19:13.244
Don't rush into it.

19:13.244 --> 19:15.814
The battles will continue
for much longer.

19:15.814 --> 19:19.384
There'll be other opportunities for
us to fight alongside each other.

19:19.384 --> 19:20.324
By that time...

19:20.324 --> 19:23.724
...I might be fighting
under your command!

19:24.724 --> 19:25.384
Commander...

19:26.064 --> 19:29.064
I wish you luck,
Deca-Commander Abriel.

19:29.064 --> 19:31.734
And the next time
we fight together...

19:31.734 --> 19:34.534
...let's empty that bottle of wine.

19:37.774 --> 19:39.344
Gates are fully open!

19:39.344 --> 19:40.634
Request permission to depart.

19:41.514 --> 19:43.244
Senior Aviator,
do you care for a drink?

19:43.244 --> 19:46.644
A little something to
celebrate our survival?

19:46.644 --> 19:48.954
That would be nice,
Line Wing Aviator.

19:48.954 --> 19:49.554
But this time...

19:49.554 --> 19:51.524
...try not to pass out on me.

19:51.524 --> 19:53.484
Forcing that medicine
down your throat...

19:53.484 --> 19:55.724
...isn't something
I want to do again.

19:55.724 --> 19:57.284
I'll be fine!

19:57.894 --> 19:59.124
What about the cat?

19:59.124 --> 20:01.564
I can't bring him along
this time.

20:01.564 --> 20:04.464
So this will be the last trip.

20:04.664 --> 20:06.534
Play with him if you like.

20:08.504 --> 20:11.774
It was strongly suggested
that going into battle...

20:11.774 --> 20:14.534
...with a cat on board wasn't
really a good idea.

20:15.814 --> 20:17.944
I hope you're not trying to
blame me for this.

20:17.944 --> 20:19.534
Of course not!

20:19.814 --> 20:20.974
But...

20:21.154 --> 20:22.484
I, uh...

20:23.184 --> 20:24.314
What can I say?

20:26.224 --> 20:28.684
I wonder who I am.

20:29.324 --> 20:31.484
I still can't find
the answer to that.

20:32.264 --> 20:34.464
But Lafiel...

20:34.464 --> 20:37.024
...there's something else
I need to find now.

20:38.264 --> 20:41.104
What you told me then...

20:41.104 --> 20:43.074
...I haven't responded to yet.

20:44.274 --> 20:46.904
But you know what, Lafiel?

20:47.204 --> 20:49.234
I'll be sure to find those words.

20:49.474 --> 20:50.874
The things I want to tell you.

20:52.144 --> 20:54.984
Until then, I'd like you
to stick around.

20:56.184 --> 20:58.614
Until the day that I can
respond to you.

21:01.724 --> 21:03.894
All engines normal.

21:03.894 --> 21:05.884
Onboard environment normal.

21:06.024 --> 21:09.584
We've been cleared for departure
from Vobeirunei traffic control.

21:10.094 --> 21:11.694
Preparations for departure
are complete!

21:12.204 --> 21:13.394
Main engine ignition!

21:13.904 --> 21:15.394
Main engine ignition!

21:21.044 --> 21:23.104
The attack vessel Basroil.

21:24.044 --> 21:24.874
Daisiele!

21:43.764 --> 21:49.104
Banner of the Stars

21:54.614 --> 21:58.174
kizukanai koto ga
The things I did not notice

21:59.614 --> 22:03.274
konnani takusan aru
I didn't know there were so many

22:05.054 --> 22:08.614
kyoumade no jibun ga
I think of myself until today

22:09.954 --> 22:13.724
nasakenaku omoete
To be so pathetic

22:13.894 --> 22:16.164
kuyashii kurai
It's almost frustrating

22:16.164 --> 22:19.364
haritsumeta kimochi ga
This tense feeling

22:21.374 --> 22:26.674
massugu ni muite ireba
As long as I keep facing forward

22:26.674 --> 22:29.704
setsunasa no nukumori
This momentary warmth

22:30.614 --> 22:34.014
hajimete shitta
I understood it for the first time

22:35.054 --> 22:39.524
kimi ga iruto
When you are there

22:39.524 --> 22:46.794
itsumo pink no namida ga nagareteru
The pink tears are always flowing

22:46.794 --> 22:51.964
kono mune no naka wo afureteru
My heart is brimming with it

22:51.964 --> 22:59.934
kimi ga dokoni itemo dareto hanashitemo
Wherever you are and whoever you talk to

23:02.514 --> 23:07.784
issho ni itaiyo soba ni ite
I want to be with you, to be near you

23:07.784 --> 23:12.824
tsunaida te kara yubisaki kara
From our linked hands and our finger tips

23:12.824 --> 23:20.884
karadajuu no omoi binetsu tsutawatte
My body heat transmits the feelings inside

23:21.764 --> 23:25.894
tomerarenai
And I cannot stop it

23:31.974 --> 23:33.804
Are you all right, Jinto?

23:33.804 --> 23:36.674
I was okay until just now.

23:36.674 --> 23:39.144
But I can't say for sure anymore.

23:39.144 --> 23:41.554
You fool. Would you have preferred
that I didn't come?

23:41.554 --> 23:43.244
Of course not.

23:43.584 --> 23:46.244
Thank you. If you hadn't come,
I'd be dead.

23:46.484 --> 23:49.494
What is it with you and your
fascination with vacuums?

23:49.494 --> 23:50.654
Give me a break.

23:50.654 --> 23:52.284
I hate vacuums.

23:52.724 --> 23:56.064
I mean, Landers like me...

23:56.064 --> 23:59.154
...have this idea that vacuums
aren't very good for you.

23:59.804 --> 24:02.204
Maybe that's just a superstition.

24:03.174 --> 24:04.944
You once said...

24:04.944 --> 24:07.944
...that you didn't think
anyone would miss you...

24:07.944 --> 24:10.274
...or grieve over your passing.

24:10.274 --> 24:12.414
What?

24:12.414 --> 24:13.434
Yeah...

24:22.594 --> 24:23.754
If you were to die...

24:24.594 --> 24:26.064
...I would be saddened.

24:26.664 --> 24:28.154
Is that insufficient?

24:38.774 --> 24:54.814
O Stars, listen to our plea
as our lives are but short.
Our wish is that you will guide us
to you when we meet our end.

24:55.724 --> 25:00.324
From the National Anthem
of the Humankind Empire Abh.
